  "sourceInstructions": "<root xmlns=\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/2004/07/adventure-works/ProductModelManuInstructions\">AI-generated fictional demo instructions. Not validated engineering or safety instructions. Down Tube (Product Number DT-2377) part sheet. Fictional shop-floor demonstration for manufacturing Down Tube DT-2377, product 327, from its direct sheet-material component.<Location LocationID=\"10\" SetupHours=\"0.15\" LaborHours=\"0.4\" MachineHours=\"0.2\" LotSize=\"1\">Work Center 10 - Frame Forming. Demo assumption: this part has no historical routing, so this existing work centre was assigned for demonstration only. Estimates are fictional demo assumptions. Frame Forming: prepare and form the sheet into the assumed tube shape.<step>Select 1.00 EA of <material>Metal Sheet 3 (Product Number MS-1256)</material> and check the sheet for visible damage.</step><step>Using an assumed <tool>sheet-cutting tool</tool>, prepare the sheet for forming; the blank dimensions are not supplied.</step><step>Use an assumed <tool>sheet-forming machine</tool> to roll the blank into a tube with the long edges meeting. See illustration <diag>2003271</diag>.</step></Location><Location LocationID=\"20\" SetupHours=\"0.1\" LaborHours=\"0.3\" MachineHours=\"0.1\" LotSize=\"1\">Work Center 20 - Frame Welding. Demo assumption: this part has no historical routing, so this existing work centre was assigned for demonstration only. Estimates are fictional demo assumptions. Frame Welding: join the assumed longitudinal seam of the formed tube.<step>Hold the formed tube in an assumed <tool>welding fixture</tool> and align its meeting edges.</step><step>Join the longitudinal seam using assumed <tool>welding equipment</tool>; welding method and settings are not supplied.</step><step>After cooling, visually check the seam for obvious gaps or damage.</step></Location><Location LocationID=\"30\" SetupHours=\"0.05\" LaborHours=\"0.2\" MachineHours=\"0.0\" LotSize=\"1\">Work Center 30 - Debur and Polish. Demo assumption: this part has no historical routing, so this existing work centre was assigned for demonstration only. Estimates are fictional demo assumptions. Debur and Polish: remove sharp edges and perform a simple visual check.<step>Use an assumed <tool>hand deburring tool</tool> to remove sharp edges from the tube ends and seam.</step><step>Visually check the finished tube for obvious surface damage and remaining burrs; set aside any questionable part for review.</step></Location></root>",
